### Theorem DGE

Let `AC` and `BD` be vertex-disjoint actual diameter edges whose projective directions are consecutive in the cyclic order of the **complete actual diameter graph**. Then

\[
\boxed{
\theta>4\arcsin\frac1{2D}.
}
\tag{DGE.1}
\]

### Theorem ESN — uniform strict improvement beyond ENS

There exists an absolute constant

\[
\boxed{\eta_E>0}
\]

such that every sufficiently large audited post-ZF survivor satisfies

\[
\boxed{
\frac{e_{BB}+2s_C}{D}
\ge
\lambda_E+\eta_E.
}
\tag{ESN.1}
\]

The gap is currently nonconstructive. The explicit floor `0.48072358047` remains valid; ESN proves that it is not the true asymptotic frontier.

